-- title:
--   A Gaussian location-mixture law is convolution with a standard Gaussian
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge0$ be an integer and let $\mu$ be a Borel probability measure on $\mathbb R^d$. Let $P_\mu$ be the Gaussian location-mixture law generated by first drawing $U\sim\mu$ and then adding independent standard Gaussian noise $Z\sim N(0,I_d)$. Then
--   $$
--   P_\mu=\mu*N(0,I_d)
--   =(\mu\otimes N(0,I_d))\circ[(u,z)\mapsto u+z]^{-1}.
--   $$
--
--   This identifies the generative mixture construction with convolution, making characteristic-function arguments available without compact-support assumptions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianIdentifiability.lean#L31-L47

